/**
@mainpage litepgo C++ API

litepgo is a C++20 library for geometry processing, finite-element elasticity,
surface contact, and sparse optimization. This reference indexes the public
headers. The <a href="../../index.html">user manual</a> explains numerical conventions,
formulations, and complete paired C++/Python examples.

@section cpp_modules Find a module

- litepgo::mesh: topology, geometry, boundary extraction, and file I/O.
- litepgo::dof: gather/scatter layouts, fixed/free reduction, and surface maps.
- litepgo::energy: scalar objectives, vector responses, composition, and assembly.
- litepgo::fem: fields, bases, quadrature, solid/shell models, and force responses.
- litepgo::solver: constrained Newton, Gauss-Newton, and equilibrium sensitivity.
- litepgo::linalg: sparse factorization backends.
- litepgo::contact: native IPC and the optional IPC Toolkit backend.
- litepgo::spatial: generic AABB spatial hashing.

Fundamental types and build information live in the root litepgo namespace.
Link the CMake module targets used by your application; I/O and the optional
Toolkit target are separate from the base aggregate.

@section cpp_contracts Before evaluating derivatives

Unknowns are scalar vectors. Vertex coordinates are packed vertex-major xyz;
material matrices are vectorized column-major. Refresh an energy/response's
sparse pattern before standalone second/first derivative assembly, respectively.
Keep borrowed C++ field inputs alive. Consult the manual for geometric domains,
force signs, physical Hermite DOFs, and local integration measures.

The source browser shows ordinary header comments as well as declarations.
Generated pages are rebuilt from headers and should not be edited directly.
*/
